          "worked": "In triangle $ABD$, $AB=2$, $BD=1$ and $AD=\\sqrt3$. For $30^\\circ$ at $A$, opposite is $BD$ and adjacent is $AD$; for $60^\\circ$ at $B$, these roles reverse.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin30^\\circ&=\\frac{BD}{AB}=\\frac12\\\\\\sin60^\\circ&=\\frac{AD}{AB}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\cos30^\\circ&=\\frac{AD}{AB}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\cos60^\\circ&=\\frac{BD}{AB}=\\frac12\\\\\\tan30^\\circ&=\\frac{BD}{AD}=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\\\\\tan60^\\circ&=\\frac{AD}{BD}=\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
